# Cloned reference repos (brownfield ingest sources)
# Exception: .references/schemas/ is tracked (S-3.7.00 derivation outputs)
.references/*
!.references/schemas
.references/schemas/*
!.references/schemas/armis
!.references/schemas/crowdstrike
.references/schemas/armis/*
!.references/schemas/armis/*.rs
!.references/schemas/armis/*.md
.references/schemas/crowdstrike/*
!.references/schemas/crowdstrike/*.rs
!.references/schemas/crowdstrike/*.md

# Factory artifacts live on factory-artifacts branch, not main
.factory/

# Claude Code local settings (use `git add -f .claude/settings.json` to share team settings)
# Exception: project skills are shared tooling, not machine-local settings
# Note: .claude/* (glob) rather than .claude/ (dir) so the !.claude/skills/ negation is evaluated.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/

# MCP server config — contains API keys, must not be committed
.mcp.json

# Rust build artifacts
target/

# Fuzz testing outputs (generated by cargo fuzz / devops smoke runs)
# These are large and environment-specific — not committed.
fuzz/corpus/
fuzz/artifacts/
fuzz/Cargo.lock

# Plugin sub-crates (standalone, not in workspace).
# NOTE: plugin Cargo.lock IS tracked (F-MCPRS-PRL10-OBS-001, human ruling 2026-07-14).
# Rationale: plugins ship as compiled binaries (.prx); locking transitive deps is the
# same app-binary concern as locking the main workspace binary. Tracking the lockfile
# closes the transitive-dep drift vector in the staleness gate (hash-plugin-source.py
# uses git ls-files, so the lockfile is included in the source-tree hash).
# NOTE: perimeter-violation/, non-exhaustive-violation/, and no-hardcoded-sensors/
# Cargo.lock files ARE tracked to pin transitive deps (e.g. tinyvec) to versions
# compatible with the pinned toolchain.
# fuzz/ Cargo.lock remains excluded (not a shipped binary); toolchain-compat pins
# (tinyvec, brotli, alloc-stdlib) are declared directly in fuzz/Cargo.toml instead.

# prism-dtu-demo-server runtime sidecars (written to cwd by `start` / `start-multi`).
# These are ephemeral process state, not source — never committed.
.prism-dtu-demo-server.pid
.prism-dtu-demo-server.pid.tmp
.prism-dtu-demo-server.urls*.json
.prism-dtu-demo-server.urls*.json.tmp
.prism-dtu-demo-server.admin-tokens*.json
.prism-dtu-demo-server.admin-tokens*.json.tmp

# direnv environment files — contains local env overrides, must not be committed
# .envrc* covers .envrc, .envrc.bed, .envrc.backup, .envrc.local, etc.
.envrc*

# Real-tenant / live-customer demo evidence (AD-017: customer data must never enter git).
# Convention: story demo evidence recorded against REAL sensor APIs lives in a `live/`
# subdir so it can be excluded here while normal DTU-based evidence (committed by the
# demo-recorder) remains tracked in the sibling per-AC dirs.
docs/demo-evidence/**/live/
